WEBVTT

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.220
Oh, so it's you, Garfield.

00:02:06.460 --> 00:02:07.940
Ace, I found it. I found it.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:09.540
Settle down. Found what?

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.920
Oil. Barrels of it. Millions of barrels of it.

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.480
Well, that's what you've been looking for, isn't it?

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.860
Yes, but I didn't expect to find it oozing out of the ground.

00:02:16.412 --> 00:02:17.412
Where is all this oil?

00:02:17.568 --> 00:02:19.168
You know the caves out on Ben Taylor's ranch?

00:02:19.676 --> 00:02:20.716
I know about where they are.

00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:21.816
They're afloat with it.

00:02:23.036 --> 00:02:25.036
How would oil get out there?

00:02:26.428 --> 00:02:26.928
Hey!

00:02:28.252 --> 00:02:29.992
We had an earthquake out there about a year ago.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:31.440
Do you suppose...

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:32.080
That's just what happened.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:34.140
The quake created new pressures on the pool.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.110
That's why the Metropolitan Oil Company has oil scouts like me

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.310
covering the San Pablo Fault from Canada to Mexico.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.090
And the quake was along that fault.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.290
Part of Ben Taylor's ranch lies right on it.

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:44.330
Oil.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.420
That's going to be a big thing in this country.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:49.520
It's going to be one of the biggest things in this country.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:50.900
We're going to be big with it.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:52.940
I don't get that.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.070
Look, Ace, I'll go back to the company and tell them I found some signs of oil.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.350
I'll get another six months to continue the survey.

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.470
Then I'll tell them about the oil in Taylor's caves.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:04.490
You left something out, didn't you?

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:06.660
You bet I did. You're part of the deal.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:07.780
All right, let's have it.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:13.700
Now here's Taylor's ranch. This is the Duchess' ranch.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:14.860
That's a right.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.030
The oil pool probably lies under this whole area.

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.290
Big as all that?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.430
And we've got to control every acre of it we can get our hands on.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.080
Adams Ranch and all the others.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.690
Then we'll sell the land to the company.

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:26.930
No, we sell nothing.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.540
We let the company drill the wells on a royalty basis.

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:31.880
Man, there's millions in it.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:32.740
Why, sure there is.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.860
But the fellas like Taylor won't want to sell out.

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:37.820
What are those gunfighters out there for?

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.400
You mean shoot them off their land?

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.200
Sure, shoot them off, burn them off.

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:43.210
Make life so miserable for them,

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:44.650
they'll sell out to you for bottle caps.

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.700
When are you going to leave for the East?

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:47.980
Tonight. I'll be back in two weeks.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.340
When you get back, we'll be in the oil business.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.440
And in a big way.

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:53.670
I'm going to pack. I'll see you later.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.850
On the way, I'll tell the boys I'd like to see them, will you?

00:03:55.850 --> 00:03:55.930
Sure.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:05.140
Red, I've never seen such goings on in my life.

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:10.810
Folks getting killed, families being burned off of their ranches, cattle being run off.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:14.020
If we don't get this fence mended, our cattle will stray off.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:18.120
Get your face out of that newspaper, Happy Jack, and give me a hand.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.030
Red, right or right, we got them work to do.

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.860
Chucks, the only time I get a chance to read what's going on in the world

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.860
is when I sneak a newspaper out into the open.

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.170
Hey, look at there, Red.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.720
You dare see what your aunt does to him? Look at that.

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:33.240
How to bake a cake.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:35.180
How to stay thin when eating cake.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:37.190
How to make doodads out of wallpaper.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.120
That's all for you, Happy Jack.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.760
The Duchess thinks you're quite a boy.

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:41.180
Boy?

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:41.540
Ha!

00:05:41.850 --> 00:05:43.910
I was a boy long before the Civil War read.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.720
Say, you know she scares me?

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.230
Well, don't let it get you.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:48.770
Put that paper down.

00:05:48.890 --> 00:05:49.670
Come over here and help.

00:05:49.970 --> 00:05:50.130
Yeah.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.120
Pull him tight, then run right or nail him.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.600
Don't you go tell me what to do now.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.810
Whoa! There goes my newspaper.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.470
But with a woman with a pair of scissors and an engine with a knife,

00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:23.610
I ain't ever going to get the newsreads.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.610
We'll ride over to Ben Taylor's place.

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:34.140
Maybe some fence down there.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:34.940
Yeah, maybe.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:38.160
Say, how come Ben ain't been in trouble with them raiders so far?

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.900
His daughter told me he has been warned.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:41.040
Oh, the skunks.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:42.980
Don't worry, Ben will catch up with them.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.100
I sure hope so.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:47.380
It'll hold.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.690
Well, let's ride over there.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:03.940
I'm going to ride into town, Dad.

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:08.770
And I don't like the idea of you riding around alone with all them raiders on the loose.

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:10.260
I'll keep my eyes open.

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.480
You better take a gun.

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:14.540
What makes you think they'll bother me?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.330
You can't tell what they'll do.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:19.340
Dad, you're worried about those raiders, aren't you?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:20.790
Sure I am.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.510
So is every rancher in the valley.

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.480
Would you like to sell the ranch and move into town?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:27.330
What are you talking about?

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.970
You don't know your dad very well if you think he can be...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.100
He's scared off his own land.

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:32.980
That sounds more like you, Dad.

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:35.790
The Raiders.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:39.330
Get inside.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:00.220
Thank you.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:24.090
I'll take care of everything.

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:26.930
Thanks, Red.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:29.670
Beaver, you take Anne to the Duchess.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.900
You safe with a little beaver, Miss Anne.

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:40.170
Sometimes I get so mad at that little Indian kid,

00:10:40.310 --> 00:10:41.870
I can fan his breeches for him.

00:10:43.150 --> 00:10:45.900
And there's other times I just love the little fella.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:47.850
Yes, I know how you feel, Happy Jack.

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:50.500
Come on, we've got a lot of work to do here.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.120
And we'll ride to town and make arrangements with the funeral.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:09.820
There, Happy Jack, you're the only ranch foreman I know who gets the socks down by the owner.

00:11:10.820 --> 00:11:14.520
I've been letting my toes leak out for years, ma'am, and liked it.

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:17.160
What you need is a woman's care, Happy Jack.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:22.950
Well, I... Oh, don't now, Red. Nothing like that. No. Oh, please. I'm happy just like I am.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:28.380
Maybe Happy Jack happy inside, but outside sour like green apples.

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:29.980
Now, there. There you see.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:32.080
See, there he goes, talking about my face again.

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.000
I think it's a nice face.

00:11:34.900 --> 00:11:36.480
Well, I wouldn't know about that, ma'am.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:38.950
I never have to look at it.

00:11:40.150 --> 00:11:41.670
Uh, that is, except on a shave.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.780
Red, what are we going to do about these killings?

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:47.410
Ben was a mighty good friend of ours.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:48.880
Don't let Aunt Heryl.

00:11:49.230 --> 00:11:50.470
She's asleep in the spare room.

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:53.190
Little beaver, better run along to bed now.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:54.540
Yes, lady, Duchess.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:55.320
Good night.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:55.780
Good night.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.970
Red, those rustlers have...

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.840
You've got to be stopped.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.220
They're not rustlers, Duchess.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:03.530
Not rustlers?

00:12:03.990 --> 00:12:06.530
Well, that's what I call killers that run off other folks' cattle.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:07.610
They're not running them off.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:09.360
Smart rustlers don't kill cattle.

00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.360
These raiders have been shooting them down,

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.360
driving them over cliffs and drowning them.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:15.320
Well, what do you make of it?

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:17.320
Somebody wants the land.

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.510
Well, it's nothing but range land.

00:12:19.850 --> 00:12:22.810
Oh, shucks, some of it ain't even worth as much as a dollar an acre.

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:25.000
I don't know why they want it,

00:12:25.500 --> 00:12:27.700
but I'm convinced that's the reason for all these raids.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:29.650
I'm not so sure about that.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.630
I still think it's a bunch of rustlers and probably backed by Ace Hanlon.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:34.770
Ace is in it, all right.

00:12:35.030 --> 00:12:38.050
He bought out Roberts, Judson, and Adams after the raid's on their places.

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:38.910
How do you know that?

00:12:39.220 --> 00:12:39.660
I checked.

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.240
Red ain't been losing no time.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.060
Red hasn't been losing no time, have you, Jack?

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:44.700
All right.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.180
Whatever you say Red hasn't been doing, he ain't been doing.

00:12:47.700 --> 00:12:49.940
Oh, Ace will probably make an offer on the Taylor Ranch.

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:52.580
If Ann sells to him, I'll spank her.

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.720
Well, you tell Ann not to sell at any price.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:58.200
And you keep your eyes on her because I have an idea there may be trouble around here.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.960
You mean those mangy raiders might strike...

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:01.140
They might.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.180
Oh, not if they know you live here, they won't.

00:13:03.360 --> 00:13:05.220
I'm going to try and block anything like that.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:05.500
How?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.940
By having a showdown with Mr. Ace Hanlon.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:09.700
Oh, but, Red.

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.540
If we had a sheriff here in Maverick, I'd let him handle it.

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:15.110
Since we haven't, somebody's got to uphold the law.

00:13:28.110 --> 00:13:29.820
Hey, what are we stopping here for, Red?

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:31.440
I thought you was headed for Ace Hanlon's.

00:13:31.440 --> 00:13:31.820
In a minute.

00:13:32.160 --> 00:13:33.560
Little beaver, you stay here with the horses.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:35.650
But Red, me wanna go do...

00:13:35.650 --> 00:13:37.050
Now, you do what Red tells you,

00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:38.810
or I'm gonna fan your britches for you.

00:13:39.070 --> 00:13:40.730
You do what me tell Dutchess.

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.910
I guess that'll hold you happy, Jack.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.190
Well, let me.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:54.370
I wanna see Ace Hanlon.

00:13:55.190 --> 00:13:55.870
He's busy.

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.350
Let him tell me that, Nick.

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:17.330
I've seen him riding around the country.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:29.910
I've got a business deal on, Ryder. What do you want?

00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.400
Still buying ranches, Ace?

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:32.840
What's that to you?

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:35.180
Don't ask questions, Hanlon. Answer them.

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:36.300
I'll handle this, Happy Jack.

00:14:36.900 --> 00:14:39.210
There isn't anything to handle. I buy what I want.

00:14:39.530 --> 00:14:42.310
And you only want the ranch's people to been gun-smoked into selling.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.210
Lay it on the line, Ryder.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:45.150
What are you driving, then?

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:47.880
Roberts, Judson and Adams were shot off of their ranches.

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:48.960
You bought them.

00:14:49.520 --> 00:14:50.080
Sure, I did.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:53.670
And you were just sore because you and your aunt got beat out of a couple of goodbyes.

00:14:54.060 --> 00:14:55.640
And now Ben Taylor's been shot down.

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:56.980
Oh, I hear.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.800
I think you had him shot, Ace.

00:15:01.050 --> 00:15:02.190
Why did you have Taylor killed?

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:05.690
It's easy to accuse a man of murder when you're pointing a gun at him.

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.940
If you didn't have that six-shooter, I'd beat you to a pulp for that crack.

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.880
I'm a peaceable man, Ace, but I'm going to accommodate you.

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.920
See that the rest of the boys stay out of this, Happy Jack.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.740
You got the whole wide world to work in, Red.

00:15:19.860 --> 00:15:20.820
Come on, get over there, hurry up.

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:22.400
Come on, knock his ears down, Red.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:32.060
You

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:38.620
By golly, that was the prettiest knuckle-and-elbow dance I've ever seen in my life right here.

00:16:39.148 --> 00:16:41.028
And I guess that'll teach you a lesson, my friend.

00:16:41.772 --> 00:16:42.232
Let's go.

00:16:42.604 --> 00:16:43.104
Okay.

00:16:48.812 --> 00:16:49.472
Get him in the office.

00:16:55.884 --> 00:16:59.504
Hey, dog, Gauntlet Red, you never give me a chance to do any nose knocking anymore.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.560
Shut up, I'm forgetting how to fight.

00:17:01.788 --> 00:17:03.548
You're getting too old and brittle, Happy Jack.

00:17:03.836 --> 00:17:05.596
I'm afraid pieces of it will break off.

00:17:06.204 --> 00:17:08.704
Huh, even Dutchess whippin' Happy Jack.

00:17:08.704 --> 00:17:11.704
Now, Happy Jack is gonna whippin' Little Beaver

00:17:11.704 --> 00:17:14.004
unless Little Beaver keep him quiet.

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:15.460
Thank you.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.440
Well, why didn't some of you boys step in?

00:17:17.948 --> 00:17:19.788
I tried to, but somebody floored me.

00:17:19.964 --> 00:17:22.884
Well, the next time Red Ryder hits town, I want you to put a bullet in him.

00:17:23.228 --> 00:17:24.868
Well, that ain't smarties. Let me do it.

00:17:25.372 --> 00:17:26.592
What's the matter? You afraid of them?

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:27.980
Now, you know better than that.

00:17:28.508 --> 00:17:29.988
But everybody in town knows you hate.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.920
If one of your men guns him, it's gonna cause you trouble.

00:17:33.340 --> 00:17:35.490
Yeah, I guess you're right. I got it.

00:17:36.770 --> 00:17:38.030
Here's a letter from Johnny Bennett.

00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:39.090
Who's Johnny Bennett?

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:41.340
They call him the San Antonio Kid.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:43.010
He used to do you a fare over me.

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.850
Broke and wants to borrow you a thousand dollars.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.580
What's that got to do with Red Ryder?

00:17:46.840 --> 00:17:48.980
He'll earn this thousand by rubbing Ryder out.

00:17:49.140 --> 00:17:50.630
I didn't know the kid was a killer.

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:52.220
He never had to be.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:17:54.880
He's the fastest man with a six-shooter I ever saw.

00:17:55.100 --> 00:17:56.180
Maybe he won't go for it.

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.860
He'll go for anything when he's broke.

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.740
And if we have to, we'll jump the ante.

00:18:00.476 --> 00:18:01.476
Along there's his address.

00:18:01.596 --> 00:18:03.196
Wire him 500 and tell him to come running.

00:18:18.332 --> 00:18:20.752
No cattle around here, Red. This country's as clean as a whistle.

00:18:20.912 --> 00:18:21.452
Looks like it.

00:18:21.756 --> 00:18:23.756
Little beavers do not have cattle.

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:26.980
Suppose there could be any strays in those caves?

00:18:27.484 --> 00:18:29.144
Well, as long as we're here, let's take a look, huh?

00:18:29.344 --> 00:18:29.964
That's a good idea.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.840
See ya.

00:19:11.548 --> 00:19:12.548
That was funny in here.

00:19:12.988 --> 00:19:13.928
Yeah, it sure does.

00:19:15.708 --> 00:19:17.088
Maybe new kind of skunk.

00:19:17.692 --> 00:19:20.072
Well, I'll take the old kind. I'm used to them.

00:19:32.200 --> 00:19:33.240
Happy Jack, it's oil.

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.260
It's what?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:34.920
Oil.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:35.800
Crude oil.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:36.320
Petroleum.

00:19:37.560 --> 00:19:38.700
What's it doing in here?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:40.760
Why, I always thought that oil come in barrels.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:43.840
Must be seedage from an oil pool.

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:45.840
It looks like there's plenty of it, too.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:48.360
That peculiar odor you smell is gas.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.180
You always find it where there's oil.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:53.030
Say, Rhett, can you grease a gun with that stuff?

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:54.460
Well, not the way it is.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.740
It has to be refined first.

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:56.680
Oh.

00:19:58.020 --> 00:19:59.400
What good stinkin' gas?

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:03.400
It can be mighty valuable, properly controlled, and can be very dangerous, too.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:08.100
So that's what's behind all this.

00:20:08.220 --> 00:20:09.620
That's what's behind all what, Red?

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:10.220
The oil.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:12.500
That's why Hanlon wants all the land around here.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:14.760
It looks like you're right, Red.

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.900
It didn't make sense when you said so the other night.

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.780
Gosh, they sure done an awful lot of killing to get it, ain't they?

00:20:20.340 --> 00:20:23.320
Little beaver no killing nobody for stinking gas.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:25.940
Say, now you hush your clapper, Sprout.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.250
Say, this makes Ann Taylor a rich gal, don't it?

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:29.970
Yes, sir, my...

00:20:30.030 --> 00:20:37.150
Rich now, don't you say a word about this to anyone anyone understand not even the duchess or and oh why not because I'm working out a plan

00:20:37.150 --> 00:20:42.580
I want you to follow my lead both of you. Oh sure anything you say that sure me keep quiet, too

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:48.040
Little beaver got the canteen off my saddle you bet you what do you want that for red?

00:20:48.160 --> 00:20:59.880
I want to take a sample of this crude oil back to the ranch she goes now

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.700
There she goes, cutting up the paper again.

00:21:02.140 --> 00:21:04.800
My golly, we could have declared war on the whole world,

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:06.660
but I'd never know it, not by that paper.

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:07.800
Now, now, Happy Jack.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:10.240
You'll be glad enough to eat this blueberry pie when I bake it.

00:21:10.340 --> 00:21:11.970
Ah, blueberry pie.

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.050
I've set the bread dough, Duchess.

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:20.130
Oh, thanks, Anne.

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:24.520
I was out to the cave country on your ranch today, Anne.

00:21:25.090 --> 00:21:25.870
Been out there lately?

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:27.770
Not for two or three years.

00:21:28.360 --> 00:21:29.900
Those caves are full of rattlesnakes.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:35.260
dad didn't like to have me go out there what do you plan to do with the ranch i don't know

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:41.510
sell it i guess i'll give you five thousand dollars for it if the duchess will loan me the

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:49.040
money five thousand dollars but it isn't worth that much red i think it is what do you want a

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:53.840
ranch for you never stay in one place long enough to run one well maybe i'm ready to settle down

00:21:55.110 --> 00:21:59.680
will you loan me the money oh so if ann wants to sell what do you say ann

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:02.150
I'd be a fool not to at that price.

00:22:02.530 --> 00:22:03.950
There used to be some old deeds around here.

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:06.390
If you've still got one, we might as well close this deal right now.

00:22:06.530 --> 00:22:08.570
Seems to me you're in a powerful hurry.

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:10.410
Well, after all, it's for Anne's protection.

00:22:10.630 --> 00:22:11.090
How so?

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:14.880
As long as these raiders are still around here, Anne may be the target for another attack.

00:22:15.550 --> 00:22:17.930
What if she doesn't own anything, then they won't be gunning for her.

00:22:18.140 --> 00:22:19.340
That makes sense, Anne.

00:22:19.820 --> 00:22:22.460
And any time you want the ranch back, you can have it for the same price.

00:22:22.640 --> 00:22:24.380
Oh, I won't want to buy it back. Don't worry.

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:25.690
Thanks a lot, Red.

00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:27.120
Where are those deeds?

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.280
Over there on the desk.

00:22:35.010 --> 00:22:41.950
Read that.

00:22:44.970 --> 00:22:48.650
The latest report indicates there is no substantial oil deposit in Painted Valley.

00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:53.920
If you cannot provide us with more favorable information within 60 days from the date of this letter,

00:22:54.560 --> 00:22:56.780
the preparation for your survey will be canceled.

00:22:57.820 --> 00:22:59.860
Very truly, Metropolitan Oil Company.

00:23:00.990 --> 00:23:04.150
by T.L. Stern, Chief Exploration Department.

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.510
What's wrong with that? We got nearly 60 days.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:10.020
What's wrong with it? Make where our set up.

00:23:10.530 --> 00:23:12.490
The whole oil field centers in the Taylor Ranch.

00:23:12.840 --> 00:23:15.200
If you make a move to buy up now, Red Ryder will jump you.

00:23:15.450 --> 00:23:16.350
And the company's bound...

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:17.970
Oh, don't be a fool, Garfield.

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:19.930
The San Antonio kid will take care of Ryder.

00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:22.020
Yeah, we hope he will, but he isn't here yet

00:23:22.020 --> 00:23:23.040
in the Taylor place of...

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.050
You'll buy the Taylor place at a fair price.

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:26.190
That'll check any suspicion.

00:23:26.910 --> 00:23:28.610
Suppose Miss Taylor refuses to sell.

00:23:28.930 --> 00:23:29.970
You'll offer enough so...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:31.720
She can't refuse, and do it tomorrow.

00:23:32.360 --> 00:23:32.840
All right.

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:50.800
A-Y-J-

00:24:29.720 --> 00:24:29.960
Thank you very much.

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:31.520
I have to run till tomorrow to get you.

00:24:37.350 --> 00:24:38.790
I'll skin you alive.

00:24:38.930 --> 00:24:40.290
I'll scalp you.

00:24:41.630 --> 00:24:43.090
I'll start a mending war.

00:24:44.280 --> 00:24:47.240
Because your ranch is precisely the type of place I'm looking for,

00:24:47.580 --> 00:24:49.780
I'm prepared to offer you $10,000 for it.

00:24:50.460 --> 00:24:51.280
$10,000?

00:24:51.840 --> 00:24:54.220
If you knew anything about land values around here,

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:56.000
you'd know that's more than the place is worth.

00:24:56.560 --> 00:24:57.840
Well, it's worth it to me.

00:24:58.400 --> 00:24:59.960
My doctor's ordered a change of class.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:03.480
Painted Valley's my choice. What's your answer, Miss Taylor?

00:25:04.450 --> 00:25:05.210
I'll take it.

00:25:05.330 --> 00:25:07.210
Good. Now, if you'll just sign this deed.

00:25:07.330 --> 00:25:07.850
She has signed it.

00:25:08.920 --> 00:25:09.380
Why not?

00:25:10.130 --> 00:25:13.020
It doesn't belong to her. My nephew, Red Ryder, owns it.

00:25:13.680 --> 00:25:14.680
Red Ryder owns it?

00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:15.260
That's right.

00:25:15.520 --> 00:25:17.540
But he said he'd sell it back to me if I wanted it.

00:25:18.120 --> 00:25:20.120
$10,000 is such a lot of money.

00:25:20.300 --> 00:25:21.340
And it'll be in cash.

00:25:21.700 --> 00:25:23.480
Red usually keeps his word, Ann.

00:25:24.610 --> 00:25:27.360
Why don't you talk to Red now? He's just riding into the yard.

00:25:32.330 --> 00:25:33.270
Hello, Ann.

00:25:33.570 --> 00:25:34.790
Hello, Dutchess.

00:25:35.010 --> 00:25:36.670
Red, this is Mr. Garfield.

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:38.470
What's he doing here?

00:25:38.650 --> 00:25:40.090
He wants to buy Ann's ranch.

00:25:40.290 --> 00:25:42.050
You'll pay me $10,000 for it.

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:44.860
I'm sorry, Ann, the ranch is for sale.

00:25:45.390 --> 00:25:48.290
But, Red, you promised you'd sell it back to me if I ever wanted it.

00:25:49.070 --> 00:25:49.830
Changed my mind.

00:25:50.010 --> 00:25:51.630
Well, you're not making much sense, Red.

00:25:52.060 --> 00:25:54.940
$10,000 is a lot of money for that ranch.

00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:57.120
Dutchess, I said the ranch isn't for sale.

00:25:57.660 --> 00:25:59.980
Apparently, some people don't hesitate at swindling their f-

00:26:00.030 --> 00:26:01.360
How much do you want?

00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:02.680
Now get this, Garfield.

00:26:03.510 --> 00:26:04.870
The Taylor Ranch isn't for sale.

00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:06.480
And you get off this one.

00:26:07.060 --> 00:26:08.460
You'll hear more from this, Ryder.

00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:09.800
I've got good ears.

00:26:10.330 --> 00:26:10.850
Now get out.

00:26:15.480 --> 00:26:17.280
Why did you treat Mr. Garfield like that?

00:26:17.850 --> 00:26:19.450
Because I don't want him on the place, Ann.

00:26:19.700 --> 00:26:20.600
I don't like it, Red.

00:26:20.780 --> 00:26:21.940
Ann can use that money.

00:26:22.140 --> 00:26:24.260
And Mr. Garfield still may want to buy.

00:26:25.160 --> 00:26:28.040
I suppose you'll sell the ranch and take the $5,000 profit.

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:34.980
Come here, little beaver. Remember that canteen I brought back from the cave?

00:26:36.230 --> 00:26:37.750
Canteen full of stinkin' gas.

00:26:37.930 --> 00:26:39.670
That's right. Well, it's hanging in the saddle room.

00:26:40.000 --> 00:26:41.640
You go get it and bring it right back here to me.

00:26:41.930 --> 00:26:42.510
You betcha.

00:26:53.420 --> 00:26:56.700
I never thought I'd see the day that Red Ryder would try to cheat a girl.

00:26:56.800 --> 00:26:58.280
Whoa, now hold on there, Duchess.

00:26:58.740 --> 00:26:59.980
Ann can't have the ranch to sell.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:02.880
because it's worth far more than any of us ever dreamed of.

00:27:03.580 --> 00:27:05.100
Red, what are you driving at?

00:27:05.380 --> 00:27:06.720
No, I'm really confused.

00:27:06.940 --> 00:27:08.620
Well, Red ain't. He knows what he's doing.

00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:10.380
Here comes stinking gas!

00:27:11.310 --> 00:27:12.150
Thanks, little beaver.

00:27:12.290 --> 00:27:21.940
See that, Ann? That's crude oil from your ranch.

00:27:22.300 --> 00:27:23.720
Crude oil? On my ranch?

00:27:23.920 --> 00:27:26.440
Those caves you haven't seen lately are practically flooded with it.

00:27:26.590 --> 00:27:27.950
That's why you didn't want Ann to sell.

00:27:28.260 --> 00:27:29.980
I didn't even want her to know about it until...

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.180
until Hanlon made his next move.

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:31.800
Hanlon?

00:27:32.360 --> 00:27:33.120
Our friend Ace.

00:27:33.340 --> 00:27:34.740
He made his move through Garfield.

00:27:35.700 --> 00:27:36.720
I'm sorry, Red.

00:27:37.280 --> 00:27:38.820
I acted like a little fool.

00:27:39.090 --> 00:27:40.110
That's all right, forget it.

00:27:41.590 --> 00:27:42.790
Who is this Garfield?

00:27:43.520 --> 00:27:44.240
I don't know yet.

00:27:44.700 --> 00:27:46.740
But he is a pal of Ace Hanlon's, isn't he?

00:27:47.410 --> 00:27:48.370
Yes, I'd call him that.

00:27:48.510 --> 00:27:49.990
Oh, if I'd known that I'd...

00:27:49.990 --> 00:27:51.310
Oh, this is a fine time to talk.

00:27:51.450 --> 00:27:52.970
Well, you've been siding with Garfield all along,

00:27:53.050 --> 00:27:55.030
and now you're trying to accuse Red of cheating Ann.

00:27:55.170 --> 00:27:56.830
Oh, you ought to be ashamed of yourself.

00:27:56.990 --> 00:27:58.450
Why, doggone it, if I was you, I'd...

00:27:58.450 --> 00:27:59.870
I tell you what I'll do.

00:28:00.060 --> 00:28:02.960
I'll grease that funeral face of yours so you can smile

00:28:02.960 --> 00:28:04.280
instead of calamity howling all the time.

00:28:04.560 --> 00:28:04.800
Oh, no, no.

00:28:04.820 --> 00:28:06.500
I've cooked your food, I've darned your socks,

00:28:06.600 --> 00:28:09.040
I've made special vittles for you, and what do I get out of it?

00:28:09.140 --> 00:28:11.700
All I've ever gotten out of you is a dismal whale of sour milk.

00:28:11.900 --> 00:28:13.020
Now come and get your oil!

00:28:13.260 --> 00:28:14.580
Come here! Come here, you!

00:28:16.840 --> 00:28:18.400
Now, now, now!

00:28:18.860 --> 00:28:21.620
Don't you just whip him, Happy Jack.

00:28:22.240 --> 00:28:24.820
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha, ha!

00:28:37.680 --> 00:28:40.980
Well, Jughead, which way do you figure Maverick is from here?

00:29:43.590 --> 00:29:45.110
Cowboy, he'll get you.

00:30:00.350 --> 00:30:01.860
Back, Thunder, back.

00:30:27.100 --> 00:30:29.970
Any time you're...

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:34.200
down in my country I'll do the same for you. Well I'll remember that. How did you

00:30:34.200 --> 00:30:38.590
get down there? Well I wasn't picking wildflowers. An eagle broke cover and

00:30:38.590 --> 00:30:45.600
scared my horse. He piled me. The best of us got thrown. I guess all my bones are in

00:30:45.600 --> 00:30:53.260
one piece. Here we go. Now look at him. Get scared by a bird, throws me four miles

00:30:53.260 --> 00:30:57.520
in the air and now he stands there as though nothing happened. Hey my name is

00:30:57.520 --> 00:30:59.640
Johnny Bennett. A red rider is mine.

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:00.580
Glad to know you.

00:31:01.050 --> 00:31:02.470
Glad he's in the work for it, brother.

00:31:03.260 --> 00:31:05.540
Say, my aunt has a ranch just over the hill here.

00:31:06.080 --> 00:31:07.060
Suppose we ride over there.

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:08.980
Maybe we can do something about this torn coat.

00:31:09.700 --> 00:31:10.420
Well, thanks.

00:31:10.600 --> 00:31:11.340
I'll be glad to.

00:31:18.970 --> 00:31:20.570
So, you're Red Ryder's pal, eh?

00:31:20.960 --> 00:31:21.660
You betcha.

00:31:21.800 --> 00:31:24.880
Red Ryder teach him Little Beaver, all Little Beaver know.

00:31:25.180 --> 00:31:27.620
Red Ryder, best cowboy in whole world.

00:31:27.910 --> 00:31:29.870
I'll put in with you there, Little Beaver.

00:31:30.860 --> 00:31:33.780
Why are you wearing six pistols tied to leg, Mr. Johnny?

00:31:34.670 --> 00:31:37.110
Sometimes I have to get to it real quick, like this.

00:31:38.420 --> 00:31:40.760
You fast, but Red Ryder faster.

00:31:41.280 --> 00:31:43.120
You sure do think a lot of Red, don't you?

00:31:43.540 --> 00:31:46.520
You betcha Red Ryder's saving little beaver's life.

00:31:47.170 --> 00:31:48.350
Little beaver never forget.

00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:51.360
I'd give a lot if somebody felt that way about me.

00:31:51.980 --> 00:31:53.460
Red's looking for you, little beaver.

00:31:54.190 --> 00:31:54.710
Me go now.

00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:58.000
Won't you have another sandwich, Mr. Bennett?

00:31:58.580 --> 00:31:59.340
No, thanks, ma'am.

00:32:00.890 --> 00:32:04.840
You know, it's worth being thrown over a cliff just to meet folks like you.

00:32:05.640 --> 00:32:07.320
But Red said you could have been badly hurt.

00:32:07.800 --> 00:32:10.440
I could have been killed, and that's bad enough for me.

00:32:14.900 --> 00:32:17.060
That jacket's seen its best days, Mr. Bennett.

00:32:17.910 --> 00:32:18.950
Red's digging you up another.

00:32:19.410 --> 00:32:20.010
Thanks, ma'am.

00:32:20.770 --> 00:32:23.530
Say, couldn't you shorten that Mr. Bennett down to Johnny?

00:32:23.790 --> 00:32:25.770
I guess we'll have to if Red has his way.

00:32:25.990 --> 00:32:27.450
He wants to keep you on the ranch.

00:32:28.290 --> 00:32:29.790
You are a cowboy, aren't you?

00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:32.180
I've punched enough cattle to be a cold one, ma'am.

00:32:32.520 --> 00:32:34.550
Well, then you've got a job, if you want it.

00:32:35.230 --> 00:32:37.570
I'd like nothing better than to work for an outfit like this.

00:32:38.230 --> 00:32:41.240
But, you see, I can make more of dealing pharaoh.

00:32:41.940 --> 00:32:42.740
Oh, a gambler.

00:32:43.450 --> 00:32:45.230
I'm not above punching cows again, ma'am.

00:32:45.920 --> 00:32:46.900
But there's something else.

00:32:47.430 --> 00:32:49.170
Are you dodging the law, Johnny?

00:32:49.520 --> 00:32:49.980
No, ma'am.

00:32:50.660 --> 00:32:53.260
I borrowed some money from a man and I promised I'd do a job for him.

00:32:54.070 --> 00:32:56.430
Oh, you don't want to tie yourself down until you've kept that promise?

00:32:56.650 --> 00:32:56.970
That's it.

00:32:57.220 --> 00:32:57.920
Good boy.

00:32:58.280 --> 00:32:58.820
Stick to it.

00:33:02.400 --> 00:33:03.280
This ought to do, Johnny.

00:33:07.450 --> 00:33:07.810
Thanks.

00:33:08.160 --> 00:33:09.560
Hey, golly, I'm glad it fits.

00:33:10.590 --> 00:33:11.630
Did you put him on the payroll?

00:33:11.850 --> 00:33:12.930
Johnny has a job to do.

00:33:13.270 --> 00:33:14.870
When he gets that done, we may see him again.

00:33:15.130 --> 00:33:15.370
Good.

00:33:15.820 --> 00:33:16.840
Oh, you'll be seeing me.

00:33:17.450 --> 00:33:19.290
Right now, I'd better be getting into Maverick.

00:33:20.240 --> 00:33:22.000
Well, thanks for everything, ma'am.

00:33:22.190 --> 00:33:23.070
Call me Duchess.

00:33:23.130 --> 00:33:23.930
Everyone else does.

00:33:26.620 --> 00:33:28.210
Well, Miss Taylor, thanks.

00:33:32.200 --> 00:33:33.680
I'll walk out to your horse with you, Johnny.

00:33:49.350 --> 00:33:51.290
Brother, what you got here is mighty fine.

00:33:52.020 --> 00:33:54.120
I haven't had anything like it since I was a kid.

00:33:54.840 --> 00:33:55.160
Folks?

00:33:55.600 --> 00:33:55.960
Cavented.

00:33:56.810 --> 00:33:58.390
Johnny, there's a job here for you anytime.

00:33:58.920 --> 00:33:59.280
Thanks.

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:00.600
There are a lot of things.

00:34:11.140 --> 00:34:11.540
Go ahead.

00:34:12.790 --> 00:34:13.330
So long, Johnny.

00:34:51.200 --> 00:34:54.860
My name is Johnny Bennett, in that office.

00:35:03.260 --> 00:35:05.920
How many times do I have to tell you to quit worrying about Red Ryder?

00:35:06.590 --> 00:35:09.540
I've always got an ace in the hole, and if I...

00:35:09.540 --> 00:35:11.300
Come in.

00:35:11.420 --> 00:35:16.720
I told you I had an ace in the hole, and here he is.

00:35:17.440 --> 00:35:18.120
Kid, how are you?

00:35:18.400 --> 00:35:19.660
Fine, ace. Just fine.

00:35:19.880 --> 00:35:21.980
Ordered. This is Johnny Bennett, the San Antonio kid.

00:35:22.220 --> 00:35:23.420
Shake hands with Mr. Garfield.

00:35:23.760 --> 00:35:24.680
Howdy, Mr. Garfield.

00:35:24.800 --> 00:35:25.400
How are you, kid?

00:35:25.960 --> 00:35:28.220
Well, I see you got my telegram.

00:35:28.620 --> 00:35:29.980
Sure. Thanks for the five minutes.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.070
I bet you haven't got much of it left.

00:35:32.350 --> 00:35:33.030
Not much.

00:35:33.530 --> 00:35:36.150
I tried to out-guess a dice game in El Paso on the way over.

00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:39.230
I told you there's only one like him.

00:35:39.590 --> 00:35:40.550
Kid, I got a job for you.

00:35:40.780 --> 00:35:41.360
Dealing Faro?

00:35:41.870 --> 00:35:43.190
Well, no, not exactly.

00:35:44.260 --> 00:35:46.290
Oh, by the way, you asked for a thousand.

00:35:49.850 --> 00:35:50.590
Here's the other 500.

00:35:51.360 --> 00:35:52.020
Thanks, Ace.

00:35:52.510 --> 00:35:53.690
There's more where that come from.

00:35:55.510 --> 00:35:56.730
Kid, I want a man rubbed out.

00:35:58.170 --> 00:35:59.770
That's a little out of my line, Ace.

00:36:00.640 --> 00:36:03.390
Look, Walt and I have got a big deal.

00:36:03.590 --> 00:36:04.750
The biggest you ever heard of.

00:36:05.470 --> 00:36:07.470
There's only one man that's standing in our way.

00:36:08.430 --> 00:36:10.030
Now, you knock him off and we'll cut you in.

00:36:10.540 --> 00:36:11.200
Sure, we will.

00:36:11.520 --> 00:36:12.980
And that thousand's only a bonus.

00:36:15.980 --> 00:36:16.560
Who's this man?

00:36:16.700 --> 00:36:18.380
His name is Red Ryder.

00:36:19.030 --> 00:36:19.650
Red Ryder.

